# Security baseline

- Never commit secrets. Use env vars only (`.env` gitignored). No API keys, Mongo URIs, or JWT secrets in code.
- Never log passwords, tokens, OTPs, full phone numbers, or raw quiz answers with PII.
- Fail closed: deny by default; allow only after authz checks.
- Validate all external input (body, query, path, headers, file uploads) with schemas.
- Do not disable security middleware "for convenience" (CORS `*`, CSRF, auth, rate limits).
- Prefer parameterized queries / ODM APIs — never string-build Mongo queries from user input.
- Return generic errors to clients; log details server-side only.
- New endpoints need: auth (if not public), rate limit, input validation, least-privilege DB access.
- Do not introduce `eval`, `exec`, `pickle.loads` on user data, or `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with unsanitized input.
- Follow `PROJECT.md` for architecture and domain rules when implementing features.
